1
00:00:01,007 --> 00:00:04,368
Part six. Results, limits, and what comes next.

2
00:00:07,468 --> 00:00:10,314
Now, the results. Here is the main one.

3
00:00:10,814 --> 00:00:21,348
On 16,000 real log lines, from eight systems the models had never seen, the team hid 1,895 sensitive values.

4
00:00:21,848 --> 00:00:26,033
Plain pattern search removed 46.1 percent of them.

5
00:00:26,533 --> 00:00:30,933
With the AI layers, Aran removed 83.5 percent.

6
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:36,308
With the normaliser and the bank's own lists, 89.7 percent.

7
00:00:36,808 --> 00:00:44,496
With the latest fixes for mobile numbers and OTPs, 91 percent, even without the bank's lists.

8
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:51,567
Aadhaar, card, PAN and UPI have been at 100 percent since the first AI version.

9
00:00:52,066 --> 00:01:01,544
False OTP alarms on 32,000 real lines: from 67,481 down to 6.

10
00:01:02,045 --> 00:01:06,485
Tokens wrongly flagged as real: zero out of 20,000.

11
00:01:06,985 --> 00:01:11,527
Leaked files traced to the right destination: 100 percent.

12
00:01:12,027 --> 00:01:20,222
Customers who could be narrowed down by joining systems: from 14,175 down to zero.

13
00:01:20,722 --> 00:01:27,169
Raw details reaching an AI company: from 100 percent down to 7.8 percent.

14
00:01:27,668 --> 00:01:39,584
Recap. Aran removes over 90 percent of sensitive values on unseen real logs, with very few false alarms, and every number type is fully protected.

15
00:01:42,084 --> 00:01:46,601
What is truly new in Aran? Good research answers this carefully.

16
00:01:47,101 --> 00:01:54,106
Card tokens that fail the Luhn check already exist in some products. That part alone is not new.

17
00:01:54,606 --> 00:02:04,066
What is new is turning it into a proven rule for Aadhaar and cards, in Theorem 1, so anyone can tell protected numbers from leaked ones.

18
00:02:04,565 --> 00:02:09,556
New: tokens that name the leaker, with a proven error rate, in Theorem 2.

19
00:02:10,056 --> 00:02:13,910
New: the OTP registry, tied to each request.

20
00:02:14,410 --> 00:02:19,343
New: the leakage ledger, which counts what joined systems can work out.

21
00:02:19,843 --> 00:02:26,804
New: one key per customer, per purpose, with signed receipts and legal time locks, in Theorem 3.

22
00:02:27,304 --> 00:02:36,043
And new: the finding that recorded traffic and a future quantum computer could undo erasure, together with the hybrid fix.

23
00:02:36,543 --> 00:02:43,404
Recap. Some single pieces exist elsewhere. Putting them together, with proofs and measurements, is new.

24
00:02:45,905 --> 00:02:51,061
Good research says plainly where it is still weak. Here are Aran's weak spots.

25
00:02:51,561 --> 00:03:00,872
Names are the weakest. About 77 percent are caught. A newer kind of AI model, called a transformer, is the planned fix.

26
00:03:01,372 --> 00:03:10,072
A transformer is the technology behind modern AI chatbots. It reads a whole sentence at once, to understand its meaning.

27
00:03:10,572 --> 00:03:20,017
After the latest fix, two new mistakes appeared. For example, a cheque number was sometimes taken for a mobile number. These must be fixed.

28
00:03:20,516 --> 00:03:30,745
Speed. Aran handles 654 log lines per second today. A big bank needs thousands per second. A faster version is planned.

29
00:03:31,245 --> 00:03:39,153
The attacks on data flows were simulated. And the AI gateway has not yet been tested with a real chatbot.

30
00:03:39,654 --> 00:03:48,027
Four of the 26 hiding tricks are still open, on purpose, because undoing them on every line would cause false alarms.

31
00:03:48,527 --> 00:03:54,285
And whether destroying a key counts as legal erasure needs a lawyer's opinion.

32
00:03:54,785 --> 00:04:02,048
Recap. Names, two new mistakes, speed, and real-world testing are the main things still to improve.

33
00:04:04,548 --> 00:04:06,199
So what comes next?

34
00:04:06,699 --> 00:04:19,576
The cybersecurity pair, Inbathamizhan and Aasif, will make the vault survive restarts, build a tracer for leaked raw numbers, and add quantum-safe connections in front of the server.

35
00:04:20,076 --> 00:04:30,516
The AI pair, Arun and Bharadhwaj, will fix the two new mistakes, add the transformer model for names, and test the gateway with a real chatbot.

36
00:04:31,017 --> 00:04:37,537
Later come Tamil name detection, reading ID card photos properly, and a research paper.

37
00:04:38,036 --> 00:04:46,906
As a product, a bank would install Aran on its own servers: as a gateway, a log cleaner, an AI gateway and a dashboard.

38
00:04:47,406 --> 00:04:52,264
It could also be offered as a service for smaller banks and finance companies.

39
00:04:52,765 --> 00:05:03,481
The timing is right. The DPDP rules begin in May 2027, and India's banking roadmap asks banks to become quantum-safe.

40
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:12,104
Recap. Fix the weak spots, make it faster, test it in the real world, and turn it into a product banks can install.

41
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:19,301
Here are questions people often ask about Aran, with short answers.

42
00:05:19,801 --> 00:05:30,649
Is this just a pattern search? No. Pattern search raised 67,481 false OTP alarms. Aran raised 6.

43
00:05:31,149 --> 00:05:42,688
Where is the AI? In finding names and addresses, telling OTPs and UPI IDs apart from look-alikes, and making every probability honest.

44
00:05:43,188 --> 00:05:52,729
Did you use real customer data? Never. The logs are real and public. Every identifier is made up, with valid check digits.

45
00:05:53,229 --> 00:06:01,926
Does tokenising break the bank's apps? No. Tokens keep the exact shape, and allowed systems can get the real value back.

46
00:06:02,426 --> 00:06:10,555
What if someone hides the number? Twelve kinds of disguise are fully caught, and 22 of 26 red team tricks.

47
00:06:11,055 --> 00:06:17,751
What if there is a typo? Typo repair catches 99.2 percent of one-typo numbers.

48
00:06:18,251 --> 00:06:29,071
How can erasure be legal, if KYC records must be kept? KYC keys are time-locked, and destroyed automatically when the legal period ends.

49
00:06:29,571 --> 00:06:34,611
Is it fast enough? Not yet, for a big bank. A faster version is planned.

50
00:06:35,111 --> 00:06:41,772
Is it a product? Yes. A bank can install it on its own servers, or use it as a service.

51
00:06:42,272 --> 00:06:50,172
Recap. Aran is not just pattern search, never uses real people's data, and says plainly where it is still weak.

52
00:06:52,671 --> 00:06:55,689
Let us bring everything together in ten points.

53
00:06:56,190 --> 00:07:03,236
One. Banks leak customer data through side doors: logs, vendors, backups and AI chatbots.

54
00:07:03,736 --> 00:07:16,193
Two. Pattern search drowns in false alarms. On real logs it raised 67,481 false OTP alarms. Aran raised 6.

55
00:07:16,693 --> 00:07:24,994
Three. Aran is a firewall for data. It sits at choke points, and swaps sensitive details for look-alike tokens.

56
00:07:25,494 --> 00:07:36,811
Four. Real Aadhaar and card numbers always pass their check digit. Aran's tokens always fail it. So protected and leaked numbers can be told apart.

57
00:07:37,311 --> 00:07:43,140
Five. Every destination gets its own tokens, so a leaked file names its leaker.

58
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:52,489
Six. Detection works like a detective, combining clues into an honest probability, with AI for names and addresses.

59
00:07:52,989 --> 00:07:58,358
Seven. The leakage ledger stops the pieces of a number from being joined together.

60
00:07:58,857 --> 00:08:06,465
Eight. One key per customer, per purpose. Destroying the keys erases every copy, with a signed receipt.

61
00:08:06,965 --> 00:08:12,462
Nine. The immune layer spots strange behaviour, like an insider at 2 a.m.

62
00:08:12,962 --> 00:08:18,557
Ten. Hybrid, quantum-safe locks keep erasure permanent, even in the future.

63
00:08:21,057 --> 00:08:28,747
Aran means fortress. Not a wall that stops the bank's work, but one that protects every customer inside it.

64
00:08:29,247 --> 00:08:31,664
Aran: protection you can prove.

65
00:08:32,164 --> 00:08:39,194
Built by Inbathamizhan S, Aasif Ahmed A, SN Arun Vijay and Bharadhwaj M, at KARE.

66
00:08:39,693 --> 00:08:41,366
Thank you for watching.

